\**Note:** This quest can not be started if the quest {q:Say It with Flowers|Say It with Flowers|Say It with Flowers} or Mission {M:The Price of Peace|The Price of Peace|The Price of Peace} has been started.
=2 Walkthrough
Before starting, check if {n:Kerutoto} keeps asking about challenging {p:Diabolos}. If she does, you will **have** to accept the quest. Once you accepted it and have {q:Waking Dreams|Waking Dreams|Waking Dreams} in your Quest Log, you'll be able to start Food for Thought.{br}{br} To receive this quest, you will have to talk to the following NPCs in this exact order:
* Speak to {n:Ohbiru-Dohbiru} in the southern **Rhinostery** building at (J-9). He will mention that he's hungry.
* Head to the northern **Rhinostery** building and speak to {n:Kerutoto}. The quest will be added to your Quest Log.
* Speak to {n:Ohbiru-Dohbiru} & {n:Kenapa-Keppa} again to get their food orders.
* Trade {n:Kerutoto} a {i:Grilled Hare|Grilled Hare|4371}.
* Trade {n:Kenapa-Keppa} a {i:Hard-boiled Egg|Hard-boiled Egg|4409}.
* Trade {n:Ohbiru-Dohbiru} a {i:Pamtam Kelp|Pamtam Kelp|624}, {i:Tortilla|Tortilla|4408}, and {i:Windurstian Tea|Windurstian Tea|4493}.
* **(!UPDATE!)** No need to speak with {n:Kerutoto}. The quest will be automatically completed once you trade the final orders.

Each item traded to the NPCs nets you a portion of the 1,000 Gil reward.
